{
  "message": "Good news: both local checks passed on design revision 2. They were \"Stateful emulator resource setup\" and \"Generated retrieval, conditional writes, ACLs, updates, deletion and revocation\". That's local evidence that the generated code handles permission filtering, updates, deletions and revocation, using simulated AWS services and scripted model replies. It doesn't prove IAM enforcement, real sign-in or MFA, API Gateway or CloudFront behaviour, how good real Bedrock answers are, or that anything can be deployed. I don't see a design defect to fix, so the board stays as it is.\n\nThe biggest open gap is that we haven't picked a country or region. Without one we can't check that your Bedrock model is actually offered there or run a provider-validated Terraform plan. Which country do the synthetic data and its processing need to stay in?",
